  "source_review": "# S15 P36 N022 combo migration \u2014 in progress\n\nBase commit: 21fee549984a74ff0dae7c42aa80c671118e6de2.\nXP commit: a2f6d7c93aa4f11efc51147566d5961c59a8ef89.\ncombo.c XP blob: f79ac6886fbdfe6b6022d1004565272f9b45bef6.\nOpenNT blob: de000921ecc635a2e282a7d6472863ada31abd35.\n\n## Source and dependency disposition\n\nThe complete combo.c algorithm is XP original. Five COLOR_HOTTRACKING arms\nand one LATER arm preserve their original guards with #error bodies; each\n#line resumes after endif, including the selected false path. The old literal\n#if 0 declaration no longer exists in XP. No behavior is removed to ease build.\n\nCBOX/COMBOWND move from the old usercli.h location to XP's inc/user.h owner;\nthere is one structure definition. Original CBNcCreateHandler,\nxxxCBCreateHandler and xxxCBCalcControlRects supply the paired XP creation,\nANSI input and right-to-left placement behavior. The rest of comboini.c,\nuser.h and usercli.h remain OpenNT-baselined prerequisites, not completed\nwhole-file migrations. Original DbcsCombine is restored in editec.c, using\nthe already bound PeekMessageA and existing queue, with no new byte buffer.\nTHREAD_CODEPAGE reuses OpenNtUserThreadCodePage and native keyboard layout.\n\nXP CB_GETCOMBOBOXINFO calls the existing retained-state info provider. The\nno-edit case is not missing a child: original comboini sets spwndEdit to the\ncombo itself. Native GetComboBoxInfo must not inspect a different private\ncontrol implementation. Existing scoped native calls now also cover\nAnimateWindow and NotifyWinEvent. Monitor geometry and UI-effect preferences\nare inputs to the existing per-call context; no second lifecycle owner.\n\nSource review found registered_init_task accepted but discarded compat_flags\nand user_flags supplied by XP wkman.c. Both now flow through the existing\nlifecycle provider to queue.c's task/client state before task insertion.\nThe XP COMPATFLAGS2_FORWOW mask is preserved. It excludes ANIMATIONOFF;\nthis change does not invent that flag for WOW. Original GetAppCompatFlags2\nis restored in winmgrc.c. No native PEB/private CLIENTINFO reinterpretation.\n\nThe combo-only _CreateWindowEx boundary adopts XP's thirteen arguments and\nRTL styles. The generic fourteen-argument WOW creation boundary is unchanged.\nThe obsolete rejected-WOW-words combo test is removed because the parameter\nno longer exists; other failure and ownership assertions remain.\n\n## Verification status\n\nLocal byte comparison proves combo.c matches XP outside six excluded arms\nand their diagnostic mappings. The first cached full build passed. The first\npublication attempt stopped at an occupied NTVDMD.DLL; the verified O:/WINNT\ninstances were terminated under existing authority. Restaging the same output\nwas rejected because the staging tool requires a fresh root. Publication from\nthe already completed runtime39 then passed all26 destination hashes.\n\nThe control cohort failed to link its standalone button fixture: the newly\nbound NotifyWinEvent boundary lacked that fixture's native forwarding function.\nNo fixture executed in that attempt. The test forwarding function is now paired;\nproduction NotifyWinEvent also uses the existing native HWND conversion before\nthe scoped call, matching other mapped native calls. Neither correction changes\nmirror diff. A second cached build and fresh runtime40 publication are pending.\nFull has not run; its first coordinator correctly stopped at the failed cohort.\n\nExisting fixtures assert explicit compatibility flags and the original WOW mask,\nand exercise actual CB_GETCOMBOBOXINFO and dropdown show/hide messages. Their\nmodified versions still require passing results. P36 is not committed or pushed.\n\n## Provisional mixed-baseline census\n\nBefore: 1329 files; 781 byte-identical; 792 nonerror-identical / 537 different;\n7848 nonerror points / 123546 changed lines.\nLocal: 1329; 781; 792 / 537; 7853 points / 119031 lines.\nDelta: zero in all file counts; +5 points / -4515 lines.\ncombo.c alone: OpenNT 1/4601 -> XP 6/6, all six remaining lines are #line.\nEight paired files retain their registered OpenNT baseline. Local census\nrecords 1273 XP / 56 OpenNT; delivered census is unchanged until acceptance.\nPoint expansion comes from original LF restoration. Final source hashes and\npublished-package tests must replace these provisional figures at delivery.\n\n## Paired message-table correction\n\nThe first runtime40 native-creation test executed the new combo info message\nthrough the real window procedure and failed both return and output assertions.\nTask-order and task-lifecycle tests had passed. The existing server.c original\nmessage bitmap omitted CB_GETCOMBOBOXINFO, so FWINDOWMSG rejected it before\nXP ComboBoxWndProcWorker. The complete pinned XP gawComboWndProc array is now\nrestored in its original C owner, including mouse-leave, style and UI-state\nmessages. No filter bypass or alternate dispatch is added. The unchanged rest\nof server.c remains OpenNT-baselined. Its nonerror metric changes from1/3010\nto1/3017; the paired unit has original XP mapping and restores the following\nOpenNT diagnostic line. P36 now affects nine mirrored files.\n\nThe runtime41 cached build/publication and affected control/native-creation/\nwindow-borrow tests are pending. Previously passed task-order/task-lifecycle\nassertions do not use this message array and retain their evidence. Full has\nnot started; the failed prerequisites are not passes.",
